---
import RosterEaseLayout from "../layouts/RosterEaseLayout.astro";
import { EULA_URL } from "../lib/rosterease";
---

<RosterEaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="RosterEase uses Apple's standard licence agreement. Find subscription information, beta guidance and privacy links."
>
  <div class="re-shell">
    <section class="re-page-intro">
      <p class="re-kicker">Terms of Use</p><h1>
        Clear terms.<br />In one place.
      </h1><p>
        RosterEase uses Apple’s standard End User Licence Agreement for its App
        Store app.
      </p><a class="re-text-link" href={EULA_URL}
        >Read Apple’s standard EULA ↗</a>
    </section><article class="re-prose">
      <section>
        <h2>RosterEase Plus</h2><p>
          Free includes one workplace in Shifts and five active clients in
          Visits. Shift Plus unlocks more workplaces and the Shift Plus
          features. Visits Plus unlocks more active clients and includes Shift
          Plus. Each plan is monthly or annual, with the same features for
          either billing period. Finishing setup for the first time gives a
          week of full Plus at no charge, which does not renew.
        </p><p>
          App Store purchases are handled by Apple. Review the in-app purchase
          sheet for your local price, billing period and any trial eligibility.
          Subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled through your Apple
          account. Use Apple’s subscription settings to manage or cancel a
          subscription, and the app’s restore option to recover eligible
          purchases.
        </p><p>
          <a href="https://support.apple.com/118428"
            >How to cancel an Apple subscription ↗</a>
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>During TestFlight testing</h2><p>
          Beta builds can change and may contain errors. Features, access and
          appearance can differ from the current App Store version. Keep backups
          and verify important schedule details against their source.
        </p><p>
          Testing is also subject to Apple’s TestFlight terms. Nothing in this
          notice excludes rights that cannot be excluded under applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Your information and support</h2><p>
          The <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains local data, optional
          sharing, backups and support information. If something is unclear, <a
            href="/contact/">contact RosterEase support</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</RosterEaseLayout>
